// intro_wake_room — first room of the intro sequence.
//
// Beat: Wake / control handoff. Player wakes on the diagnostic cart
// in the creator's basement lab. Creator says "Hey you, you're
// finally awake."
//
// The cart (2026-10-10): the cart is not a prop on a platform. Its bed IS
// the platform: a `MovingPlatform` that stands still (`speed: 0`), one-way,
// drawn as the sheet `intro_cart`. The near rail of the cart is drawn in
// front of each body, so the player wakes IN the cart. Its back end is a
// ramp: one still `MovingPlatform` that carries the ramp's picture (the
// sheet's `ramp` row), and a hidden `SurfaceChain` (`Cart ramp`) from the end
// of the bed to the floor, which a body walks (`walkable_lines`; until
// 2026-10-15 the ramp was 14 one-way steps of 4).
//
// ⚠ The map was changed with the entity tools after this spec made the
// room. This spec has the cart, the spawn and the landing pad of the map,
// and it does NOT have the ramp. The map is the authority: do not make the
// room again from this spec.
//
// Transitions:
// - Incoming: the door of the hub (sandbox.ldtk, `intro_wake_door`) is one
//   way. It arrives at `wake_room_arrival`, a landing pad on the bed of the
//   cart that names no target and has no picture.
// - Outgoing: right-edge EdgeExit zone `wake_to_raid` (a thin slice
//   at x=1008) so walking off the right edge scrolls into
//   `intro_raid_corridor` without a door prompt. EdgeExit is the
//   sandbox's walk-through equivalent — no Interact press required.
//
// Layout (1024×384):
//
//   +-------------------------------------------------+
//   | ▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒ ceiling ▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒ |
//   |                                                 |
//   |                                                 |
//   |   ▢[cart+player]    [Creator]               →→  | ← right
//   |▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒│   edge exit
//   +-------------------------------------------------+

